  "privacyHeading": "Your Copies, Your Privacy",
  "privacyTitle": "Your photos always belong to you.",
  "privacyBody": "Your photos go to a bucket you own, as ordinary files. Alongside them sits an index.csv listing every photo by date, album, person, caption and place — so you can find any one of them again with a spreadsheet and nothing else. No account, no export tool, no us. The app deletes from your bucket only to carry out what you asked: deleting a photo, hiding or un-hiding one (the old copy goes once the new one is in every bucket), or a fix you confirm.\n\nNothing is ever sent to the developer. There is no server and no account: your library, its records and its face data stay in a database on this iPhone, and all processing — grouping, search, face recognition — happens here. Photos go only where you send them: your own bucket or your own iCloud. Keys are kept in the Keychain, never in the app's own backups; like every Keychain item, they are part of an encrypted iPhone backup.",
