  "privateAlbumBackupStatusOff": "No bucket set up, so this phone holds the only copy — encrypted, but the only one.",
  "privateAlbumBackupExplainer": "Hiding removes a photo from Photos. This app keeps it on this phone in a folder that is left out of your iPhone backup, under a name that says nothing — so the album works with no internet and no bucket at all.\n\nWith a bucket, an encrypted copy goes up inside a file that opens as an ordinary picture; only your passphrase and code open the real photo. That is the copy that survives losing the phone, or restoring it from a backup. The app's database keeps a row for each hidden photo, under a tag of its code that can't be turned back into the code without a key in the Keychain. The app-data backups — Files, iCloud Drive, your bucket — leave hidden photos out; their notes go sealed.\n\nSelect photos in the album to send their full copies back to the bucket and free up space here. Their tiles stay, and opening one downloads it again.",
