  "collectionsDeveloperRow": "Developer Options",
  "devTitle": "Developer Options",
  "devIntro": "Bring data in from files made outside the app. Every import shows what it will change before writing anything, and running the same file twice adds nothing new.",
  "devSectionPeople": "People",
  "devSectionFaces": "Faces",
  "devSectionChats": "Chats",
  "devHowItWorks": "How it works",
  "devFileSpec": "File format",
  "devChooseFile": "Choose File…",
  "devExportNow": "Export…",
  "devCsvImportTitle": "Import Profiles",
  "devCsvImportSummary": "Add or update people from a spreadsheet.",
  "devCsvImportHow": "• Each row is one person, matched to people already here by name, ignoring case.\n• New names become new people; matched ones are updated.\n• By default the file's values win, lists only grow, and First met / Last seen only widen. A row's mode column changes that.\n• You see every addition, update and conflict before anything is saved.\n• Photos aren't touched.",
  "devCsvImportSpec": "File: .csv, UTF-8, comma-separated, header row first.\n\nColumns (only name is required, the rest in any order; unknown columns are ignored; header spelling is loose: \"Birth Date\" = birth_date = birthdate):\nname, firstname, middlename, lastname, birthdate, gender, bio, firstmet, lastseen, hair, eyes, height, build, handed, languages, diet, contact, …, fields, groups, education, jobs, places, tags, mode\n\nDates: 2019, 2019-06 or 2019-06-14.\ngender: male or female.\n\nLists: items split by ;  and an item's parts split by |\n• fields: Label|Value; Label|Value\n• groups: Name|kind (kind: family, company, school or circle; circle if left out)\n• education, jobs: Title|Detail|Start|End (only Title required)\n• places, tags: plain items\n\nmode (per row):\n• empty: merge as above\n• all: the profile becomes exactly the row\n• conflict: the row wins where they differ, nothing removed\n• skip: what's here wins, the row only fills blanks",
  "devCsvExportTitle": "Export Profiles",
  "devCsvExportSummary": "Everyone as a .csv, in the same format Import reads.",
  "devCsvExportHow": "• Writes one row per person with every column above, then opens the share sheet.\n• Hidden people stay out.\n• Edit it in any spreadsheet and import it back to update profiles in bulk.",
  "devZipTitle": "Import People Zip",
  "devZipSummary": "Profiles and each person's photos in one archive.",
  "devZipHow": "• Step 1: tick whose profiles to add or update (from people.csv, if the zip has one).\n• Step 2: pick photos per person, already in People. Each person has an Import tick and a Hide tick.\n• Imported photos go to Archive and the person's page, never the main grid. Ticked Hide puts them in that person's hidden folder behind a code.\n• Folders never create people: a folder whose name matches nobody is greyed out.\n• Same photo twice is skipped. Big libraries: split into ~500 MB zips and import them one after another.",
  "devZipSpec": "File: .zip\n\npeople.csv              optional; the Import Profiles columns\nphotos/<name>/<file>    one folder per person\n\n• <name> must equal the person's name (ignoring case).\n• Photos: jpg, jpeg, png, gif, bmp, webp, heic, heif. Videos: mov, mp4.\n• Anything else is skipped and counted.",
  "devFacesTitle": "Import Faces File",
  "devFacesSummary": "Named faces and face groups from the Mac face tool.",
  "devFacesHow": "• Made by tools/faces on a Mac (face recognition over your bucket).\n• Photos are found by their bucket file name, or by the original's SHA-256.\n• A face with a person is named at once; boxes are matched to faces the phone found, or added.\n• Faces with a group wait under People → Faces to Name, where you check them and tap Name….\n• A suggest is only a proposal. Faces you already named, removed from a group, or groups you deleted stay as they are.\n• Hidden photos are skipped. You see the counts before anything is written.",
  "devFacesSpec": "File: faces.json, UTF-8 JSON, version 1 or 2.\n\n• photos[].key: the bucket key's file name without extension; or sha256 (hex) of the original instead.\n• box: [x, y, w, h], 0–1, from the top-left of the upright photo.\n• A face has person or group, never both. group: version 2 only.\n• groups[]: id required; faces is a count; suggest optional.\n• Unknown fields are ignored; unreadable faces are skipped and counted.",
  "devChatsTitle": "Import Chat History",
  "devChatsSummary": "Messages from QQ, WeChat, SMS or WhatsApp exports, onto people.",
  "devChatsHow": "• Messages are grouped by the person's name. A name that matches someone in People is attached to them; others wait unticked until you point them at someone or make them a new person.\n• Shows each name's chats and message count before importing.\n• The same message twice is kept once, so re-importing a newer export only adds what's new.\n• Messages show on the person's page.",
  "devChatsSpec": "Files: .jsonl (one JSON object per line), or .zip files containing .jsonl. Several at once.\n\n• Required: person, at (ISO 8601, local time).\n• from_me: true for your messages; default false.\n• source: qq, wechat, sms or whatsapp; taken from chat before \":\" if missing.\n• kind: text, image, voice, file, system or other; default text.\n• Lines that aren't JSON, or lack person or at, are skipped and counted.\n• thumb: a small JPEG of the picture, video or file, in base64.",
  "devExample": "Example",
  "eventsSeenFromPhoto": "from a photo",
  "eventsSeenFromChat": "from a chat",
  "eventsSeenFromEvent": "from an event",
